From: Alberto Cavalcante <54247214+albertocavalcante@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Feb 2026 11:12:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add OnIteration callback for loop coverage
 instrumentation

Add Thread.OnIteration callback invoked after each for-loop iteration
decision (ITERJMP). This enables loop coverage collection.

The callback receives:
- fn: the executing function
- pc: program counter of the ITERJMP instruction
- continued: true if loop continues, false if loop exits

This allows tracking:
- How many times each loop iterates
- Whether loops execute 0, 1, or N iterations
- Empty loops (continued=false on first check)

Changes:
- Thread.OnIteration field in eval.go
- Callback invocation in interp.go after ITERJMP evaluation
- Tests for loop iteration counting and empty loops

